    <statement><p>Determine whether the following system has no solution, an infinite number of solutions or a unique solution.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}\amp  -7 \, x\amp +\amp  5 \, y\amp +\amp  5 \, z\amp =\amp -5\\\amp  4 \,x\amp +\amp   \, y\amp - \amp 2 \,z\amp =\amp -5\\\amp  37 \,x\amp - \amp 11 \,y\amp - \amp 23 \,z\amp =\amp -4\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}\amp  -7 \, x\amp +\amp  5 \, y\amp +\amp  5 \, z\amp =\amp -5\\\amp  4 \,x\amp +\amp   \, y\amp - \amp 2 \,z\amp =\amp -5\\\amp  37 \,x\amp - \amp 11 \,y\amp - \amp 23 \,z\amp =\amp -5\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}\amp  -4 \, x\amp - \amp 8 \,y\amp - \amp 31 \,z\amp =\amp 1\\\amp  - \, x\amp - \amp  \,y\amp - \amp 5 \,z\amp =\amp 6\\\amp  3 \,x\amp +\amp  6 \, y\amp +\amp  24 \, z\amp =\amp 6\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
